This product includes third-party software. Each dependency is listed with its
license; versions are pinned in uv.lock (Python) and package-lock.json (Node).

Python runtime dependencies
- httpx2 (BSD-3-Clause) — HTTP client for the GitHub REST API (also used by openai)
- openai (Apache-2.0) — OpenAI-compatible client used to call the Meta Model API and Baseten
- pydantic (MIT) — data models and JSON Schema generation
- Pillow (MIT-CMU) — redraws captured terminal output as PNG screenshots for the screen judge
- modal (Apache-2.0) — Modal client: runs verification sandboxes (gVisor) on Modal

Python development dependencies
- pytest (MIT)

Verification sandbox image (pickfit/verify/sandbox.Dockerfile; built locally,
not distributed with pickfit)
- python:3.12-slim Docker official image (Python: PSF-2.0; Debian packages under their own licenses)
- Node.js 22, copied from the node:22-slim image (MIT); npm (Artistic-2.0)
- uv (MIT OR Apache-2.0)
- pipx (MIT)
- slirp4netns (GPL-2.0-or-later; Debian package, run as its own program) — a gVisor box's network uplink

Node runtime dependencies (worker/, bundled into the Cloudflare Worker)
- @modelcontextprotocol/server, @modelcontextprotocol/core (Apache-2.0) — official MCP TypeScript SDK v2
- zod (MIT) — tool input and output schemas

Node development dependencies (worker/)
- wrangler (MIT OR Apache-2.0) — Cloudflare Workers CLI (local dev, D1 migrations)
- typescript (Apache-2.0)
- @types/node (MIT)

Software profiles (data/software/*.json)
- Each record is written by pickfit from public sources: repository facts from the
  GitHub REST API, and short verbatim quotes from the project's own README and
  release notes as evidence for each extracted field. Every record lists the URL of
  each source it quotes. Quoted text remains under its project's license; pickfit
  claims no rights in it.
- Popularity signals in scores are counts read from public APIs: the npm registry
  and api.npmjs.org downloads, the PyPI JSON API and pypistats.org, the crates.io
  API, Homebrew's formulae.brew.sh API, and Hacker News stories through the Algolia
  HN Search API. Only package names, counts and story scores are kept.
